                "title": "8d_report_valve_body_bore_oversize.pdf",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "8D Report: Bore Diameter Oversize on Valve Body AP-3312\nD0. Summary\nOn 14 August 2026 Brightline Hydraulics returned 48 proportional valve bodies (AP-3312) because the main bore was oversize. Between 3 August and 21 August, 12 further bore-diameter nonconformances (285 pieces) were recorded in process on the same part, all on CNC lathe MTY-LTH-04 at the Monterrey Plant. The cost of the nonconforming parts, including the customer return, was $12,844.80.\nThe root cause was a worn spindle bearing. The bearing’s vibration rose for several weeks while the machine’s PM-2 service was 12 days overdue, and the in-process gauge plan was too sparse to catch the drift. The spindle bearing failed on 24 August 2026 and the spindle cartridge was replaced. No further bore-diameter nonconformances were recorded after the repair.\nThis is a synthetic document written for a software demonstration. Atlas Precision Components, Brightline Hydraulics and every person named here are fictional.\nChampion, Name = Elena Marsh. Champion, Function = Plant Manager, Monterrey. Team leader, Name = Rafael Ocampo. Team leader, Function = Quality Engineering Manager, Monterrey. Member, Name = Dario Quintero. Member, Function = Maintenance Supervisor, Monterrey. Member, Name = Ines Valdivia. Member, Function = CNC Programmer, Monterrey. Member, Name = Tomas Reyes. Member, Function = Process Engineer, Monterrey. Customer contact, Name = Helen Park. Customer contact, Function = Supplier Quality Engineer, Brightline",
