                "chunkId": "manufacturing.reports:f-3cee2535ce10c3a6:0009",
                "title": "8d_report_valve_body_bore_oversize.pdf",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "8D Report: Bore Diameter Oversize on Valve Body AP-3312\nFive whys\nWhy was the bore oversize?, Answer = The spindle ran out of true and the cutting position drifted as the bearing wore.. Why did the bearing wear out?, Answer = The bearing reached the end of its life while the lubrication and preload checks of PM-2 were not done on time.. Why was PM-2 late?, Answer = The last PM-2 was on 14 April 2026. The 120-day interval for CNC lathes (PM-MAN-001, Table 1) made it due on 12 August 2026. The planner deferred it twice to protect the Brightline delivery.. Why was the drift not caught earlier?, Answer = The vibration warning level was exceeded for 14 days before the failure but the alert went to a shared mailbox that nobody owned.. Why did the nonconforming parts leave the plant?, Answer = The gauge plan checked one piece in 25, which cannot detect a drift of a few microns an hour.\nOccurrence, Root cause = Spindle bearing wear on MTY-LTH-04, failure code SPN-BRG.. Detection, Root cause = Gauge frequency of one piece in 25 was insufficient for a drifting process.. Systemic, Root cause = The CMMS allowed work orders to be released on a machine more than 14 days past its PM-2 interval, and vibration alerts had no owner.",
                "metadata": {
                  "parser": "nemotron-parse-2.0",
                  "file_id": "f-3cee2535ce10c3a6",
